    "## 3. Prepare Features and Target\n",
    "\n",
    "Only the combined email text is used as the input feature.\n",
    "\n",
    "The sender, receiver, date, and URL metadata are excluded so that\n",
    "the experiment focuses on text-based phishing detection."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "0af17e37-755e-4402-ac2f-cb3dacd01efb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train = train_df[\"text\"]\n",
    "y_train = train_df[\"label\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "X_val = val_df[\"text\"]\n",
    "y_val = val_df[\"label\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test = test_df[\"text\"]\n",
    "y_test = test_df[\"label\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4c3a02c3-4bbe-4a25-ac83-82e10a4d09d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. TF-IDF Feature Extraction\n",
    "\n",
    "TF-IDF is used to transform the email text into numerical features.\n",
    "\n",
    "The vectorizer is fitted exclusively on the Enron training data.\n",
    "The validation and test sets are transformed using the fitted\n",
    "vectorizer without refitting.\n",
    "\n",
    "This prevents information leakage from the evaluation sets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "846e7f12-0391-4604-b48c-24e8b36d300b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Training matrix: (20596, 100000)\n",
      "Validation matrix: (4414, 100000)\n",
      "Test matrix: (4414, 100000)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "tfidf = TfidfVectorizer(\n",
    "    lowercase=True,\n",
    "    stop_words=\"english\",\n",
    "    max_features=100000,\n",
    "    ngram_range=(1, 2),\n",
    "    min_df=2,\n",
    "    max_df=0.95,\n",
    "    sublinear_tf=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_tfidf = tfidf.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_val_tfidf = tfidf.transform(X_val)\n",
    "X_test_tfidf = tfidf.transform(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Training matrix:\", X_train_tfidf.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Validation matrix:\", X_val_tfidf.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Test matrix:\", X_test_tfidf.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a12e95c7-c3db-40dd-81e8-d293f968bffa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Linear SVM Model\n",
    "\n",
    "A Linear Support Vector Machine (SVM) is trained using the TF-IDF\n",
    "features.\n",
    "\n",
    "The SVM uses the same training data and feature representation as\n",
    "the Logistic Regression baseline, allowing a direct comparison\n",
    "between the two traditional machine-learning approaches."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "63a14563-6c47-4d7f-809d-cb32c5748d56",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Training time: 0.30 seconds\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "start_time = time.time()\n",
    "\n",
    "svm_model = LinearSVC(\n",
    "    C=1.0,\n",
    "    class_weight=\"balanced\",\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "svm_model.fit(X_train_tfidf, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "training_time = time.time() - start_time\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training time: {training_time:.2f} seconds\")"
   ]
  },
